      "message": "this is really poorly optimized on the critical path.\nThis x86 core has an hardware DIV instruction capable of doing 64-bit/32-bit division (EAX \u003d EDX:EAX/RM) ? it\u0027s just GCC doing a poor job here ?\n\nif you do this:\n        /* Force GCC to use the DIV instruction to divide by 12 */\n        uint32_t hi \u003d tmp \u003e\u003e 32;\n        uint32_t lo \u003d tmp;\n        uint32_t q, r;\n        const uint32_t d \u003d 32;\n        asm (\"divl %4\" : \"\u003dd\" (r), \"\u003da\" (q) : \"0\" (hi), \"1\" (lo), \"rm\" (d) : \"cc\");\n        return q;\n\nLooks way better on my machine, is it working for you ?",
